For simplicity, start with Option A (hardcoded). Refactor later if needed.

### What Runs Where

| Component | Environment | Has access to |
|-----------|-------------|---------------|
| rmail daemon | Standard Lua 5.1+ | Network, filesystem, hooks |
| validate-custom-class.lua | Standard Lua (child of rmail) | Filesystem, rmail outbox |
| custom-classes.lua | ALE (inside worldserver) | ALE APIs, character DB, filesystem |
| worldserver | C++ | Everything |

### Data Flow: Class Submission

```
1. User writes to ~/mail/outbox/knight.txt
2. User's rmail daemon reads outbox, connects to game server port 8025
3. Game server's rmail daemon receives, writes to /home/ritz/game-mail/inbox/
4. on_receive hook fires: lua validate-custom-class.lua "alice" "CLASS: knight" "/path/to/inbox/file"
5. Hook validates, either:
   a. Invalid: delete inbox file, write error to outbox (→ user's inbox)
   b. Valid: keep inbox file, write confirmation to outbox
6. (Later) Player creates character, ALE reads from inbox, creates snapshot
```

### Data Flow: Character Creation

```
1. Player talks to class selection NPC
2. ALE scans /home/ritz/game-mail/inbox/ for CLASS: messages
3. ALE filters by base class (stat_growth matches player's class)
4. Player selects "Knight" by alice
5. ALE reads alice's inbox file, re-validates
6. ALE copies to src/custom-class-snapshots/alice-knight-v<timestamp>.lua
7. ALE stores "alice-knight-v<timestamp>.lua" in character data
8. Character is created
```

### Data Flow: Character Login

```
1. Character logs in
2. ALE checks character data for CharCustomClassSnapshot
3. ALE loads from src/custom-class-snapshots/<snapshot>.lua
4. Character plays with that class definition
```

